  "prefLabel": "Rev 1803.03 Reserved Rights",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1803.03 Reserved Rights. The portion of conservation restriction easement land in which the landowner has reserved rights in the deed granting such easement, which allow for future inconsistent use improvements, in specified or unspecified geographic areas, including ingress and egress thereto, shall be taxable in accordance with RSA 75:1 when an inconsistent use occurs.\n\nSource. #5231, eff 9-27-91; ss by #5353, eff 3-12-92; ss by #6692, eff 2-21-98; ss by #8567, eff 2-14-06; ss by #10560, eff 3-28-14; ss by #13867, eff 2-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1800.html"
